--
N5008 [class.mi]/4: D has two A subobjects but, V being a virtual base of
A, one V subobject shared by both; [class.virtual]/2 gives each A its own
final overrider of f, and D::g is the final overrider of V::g.  The front
end rejected the class.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
